<template>
    <!-- Vue 3 ESM-bundler build needs these compile-time
         flags defined as globals before any Vue module loads.
         Inline script runs synchronously at SSR parse time,
         so the values are set by the time the browser
         dynamic-imports the VueFlow island. -->
    <script>
        window.__VUE_OPTIONS_API__ = true;
        window.__VUE_PROD_DEVTOOLS__ = false;
        window.__VUE_PROD_HYDRATION_MISMATCH_DETAILS__ = false;
    </script>
    <div class="arch">
        <h1>Architecture (VueFlow inside nl-island)</h1>
        <p class="hint">
            VueFlow + Vue 3 live inside the
            <code>&lt;nl-island/&gt;</code> below — loaded lazily from
            esm.sh, mounted once, never re-mounted by subsequent
            server-driven re-renders. The toolbar below mutates
            server-side <code>Graph</code> state; the new props blob
            flows to the island's <code>updated()</code> callback,
            which reactively swaps the nodes/edges refs. VueFlow's
            internal pan / zoom / selection state survives.
        </p>

        <div class="toolbar">
            <button @click="addNode">+ Add node</button>
            <button @click="addEdge">+ Add edge</button>
            <button @click="randomize">Randomize positions</button>
            <button @click="reset">Reset</button>
            <button @click="focusFirst">Focus first node (PushIsland)</button>
            <span class="status">
                {{ len(Graph.Nodes) }} nodes · {{ len(Graph.Edges) }} edges
            </span>
        </div>

        <nl-island name="ArchCanvas" src="/islands/vueflow-canvas.js" :props="GraphProps()"/>

        <p class="hint footnote">
            Open DevTools → Network. After the initial page load,
            <strong>no</strong> HTML re-arrives over HTTP — every
            mutation flies through the WebSocket as a sparse diff,
            and the only JS the browser ever fetches beyond
            <code>/__live/nexus.js</code> is <code>vueflow-canvas.js</code>
            plus its two esm.sh imports.
        </p>
    </div>
</template>

